  "contracts": [
    "Client.PrepareGeneration returns an ordinary generation without storage writes or active-state changes.",
    "Publisher.PrepareCatalog selects a durable sequence without reserving it; commit retains atomic CAS.",
    "WithAuthorityOrigin explicitly selects identity, policy, sole publication store, and qualified clock callback.",
    "The runtime prepares the authority identity before input journal staging, then activates those exact bytes.",
    "Ambiguous commit recovery selects the accepted authority identity and retains its accepted inputs without minting a new sequence.",
    "Unchanged reconstruction proves source identity against the accepted origin digest; bootstrap cannot reset an authority.",
    "Bootstrap runs inside the client publication guard; denied publication changes no catalog storage.",
    "Origin receipts observe the durable head independently of successful serving-client activation.",
    "Publication guards prevent direct client mutation; subscribers cannot become origins through this option."
